
Operating System Security Governance Program for Unidad Web
Project Overview

Developed an enterprise operating system security governance program for Unidad Web, a cloud services provider supporting over 5,000 clients across the eastern United States. The organization operates a hybrid infrastructure consisting of Windows, UNIX, and Linux systems that support website hosting, email services, cloud storage, and business applications.

The objective of this project was to establish a security governance framework that improves system security, reduces cybersecurity risk, supports regulatory compliance requirements, and strengthens operational resilience.

Business Scenario

Unidad Web faces multiple cybersecurity risks, including:

Ransomware attacks
Data breaches
Insider threats
Service outages
Unauthorized access attempts

These risks are particularly significant because the organization serves healthcare providers, financial institutions, and businesses that process sensitive information.

Security Architecture

The environment includes:

120 Windows 11 workstations
15 Windows Server 2022 systems
10 UNIX servers
25 Linux servers
VPN infrastructure
AWS cloud services
Microsoft 365 services

Security zones include a DMZ, internal LAN, firewall, VPN gateway, and cloud integrations.

